Source: pg-statement-rollback
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ruohang Feng <rh@vonng.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), postgresql-all (>= 217~)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/HexaCluster/pg_statement_rollback

Package: postgresql-PGVERSION-pg-statement-rollback
Architecture: any
Provides: postgresql-pg-statement-rollback
Depends: ${postgresql:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: server-side statement rollback for PostgreSQL
 pg_statement_rollback is a loadable PostgreSQL module that manages automatic
 savepoints, allowing a client to roll back a failed statement and continue
 the current transaction. It intentionally installs no CREATE EXTENSION SQL
 objects and is enabled with session_preload_libraries or LOAD.
